            <ArticleTitle>Scaling Fixed-Field Alternating-Gradient Accelerators with Reverse Bend and Spiral Edge Angle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>064802</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1103/PhysRevLett.119.064802</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel scaling type of fixed-field alternating-gradient (FFAG) accelerator is proposed that solves the major problems of conventional scaling FFAGs. This scaling FFAG accelerator combines reverse bending magnets of the radial sector type and a spiral edge angle of the spiral sector type to ensure sufficient vertical focusing without relying on extreme values of either parameter. This new concept makes it possible to design a scaling FFAG for high energy (above GeV range) applications such as a proton driver for a spallation neutron source and an accelerator driven subcritical reactor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
